From: Martyn Forryan <iamfoz@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] server: Add the LocalSystem group to the default token.

Services run with the same admin token as everything else, where on Windows
they run as LocalSystem. A process that sets a DACL on its own process
object admitting only LocalSystem is then unreachable from the service that
started it: OpenProcess() fails with STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED.

Backblaze's backup client does exactly this from 10.0.3.1075. Its service,
bzserv, opens the backup pass it launched by pid every ten seconds to check
it is alive; the pass grants access to itself only to LocalSystem; the open
is denied, bzserv concludes the pass has died, deletes the pass's lock file
and starts another, and no backup pass ever completes.

Adding NT AUTHORITY\SYSTEM as an enabled group to the token created by
token_create_admin makes such a DACL admit the service, which matches what
the process would see on Windows. The group is appended, so the primary
group index passed to create_token still names domain_users.

---
--- a/server/token.c
+++ b/server/token.c
@@ -768,6 +768,13 @@
         { &alias_admins_sid, SE_GROUP_ENABLED|SE_GROUP_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT|SE_GROUP_MANDATORY|SE_GROUP_OWNER },
         { &alias_users_sid, SE_GROUP_ENABLED|SE_GROUP_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT|SE_GROUP_MANDATORY },
         { &logon_sid, SE_GROUP_ENABLED|SE_GROUP_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT|SE_GROUP_MANDATORY|SE_GROUP_LOGON_ID },
+        /* Services run with this same token, where on Windows they run as
+         * LocalSystem. A process that grants access to itself only to
+         * LocalSystem (Backblaze's bztransmit does, and its bzserv opens it by
+         * pid to supervise it) is otherwise unreachable from the service that
+         * started it. The group goes last so the primary group index below
+         * still names domain_users. */
+        { &local_system_sid, SE_GROUP_ENABLED|SE_GROUP_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT|SE_GROUP_MANDATORY },
     };
 
     token = create_token( primary, session_id, user_sid, admin_groups, ARRAY_SIZE( admin_groups ),
